  Slug: steward-of-stone-and-fire
  DisplayName: Steward of Stone and Fire
  IconPath: icons/environment/wilderness/cave-entrance-mountain.webp
  Description: 'Stewards of stone and fire linger near volcanoes and deep places
    near the heart of the earth, hot springs where the water is too scorchingly hot
    to allow casual enjoyment, and other places where the barrier between fire and
    earth is thin or nonexistent, though particularly old rock formations, canyons,
    and other natural features of earth may also spawn or attract them. Stewards
    of stone and fire are quick to anger and slow to forget. Apparition Skills Mountain
    Lore, Volcano Lore Apparition Spells Cantrip @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Ignition]
    1st @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Interposing Earth] 2nd @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Exploding
    Earth] 3rd @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Fireball] 4th @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Wall
    of Fire] 5th @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Wall of Stone] 6th @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Petrify]
    7th @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Volcanic Eruption] 8th @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Earthquake]
    9th @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Falling Stars] Vessel Spell @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Earth''s
    Bile] Avatar Blood of Planets Speed 50 feet, burrow Speed 50 feet, ignore difficult
    terrain and greater difficult terrain Melee 1 avalanche of molten stone (reach
    15 feet, versatile B), Damage @Damage[(6d10+6)[fire]] Ranged 1 cleansing eruption
    (fire, range 120 feet), Damage @Damage[(6d6+6)[fire]]'
